pe":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"The answer covers all three requested inquiry areas. Selection: how the LMM or exchange was chosen, alternatives considered, conflicts, and ability to quote under stress. Relevant-market expertise: asset-class track record, staffing and continuity, and spread and depth metrics. Capital and seed support: whether seed is temporary inventory, the unwind plan, quoting after seed withdrawal, incentive payments, and termination terms. It separates temporary market-maker seed from investor assets expected to last. By asking what drives retention of those assets, it implies they are not guaranteed to stay. It also frames the checklist as suggested inquiry rather than a mandatory approval rule. Minor gaps: it does not say outright that subsidized or lasting investors can leave, and its seed questions slightly assume seed is offered rather than noting that not every LMM provides it. Neither gap is a material error.\"}","ttft_ms":2665,"type":"result","duration_ms":5557,"uuid":"28df4814-807c-4464-9a53-fcd2dede3a11","ttft_stream_ms":580,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":580,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
